        "original_id": "54b254d5-3db1-50ec-b594-5197efaea6a2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Miller, Patti Page, O. C. Smith\n- Songs: \"Little Green Apples\"\n- Awards: Grammy Award for Best Country Song\n- Charts: Billboard Hot 100, UK Singles Chart\n\nFacts:\n- The Grammy Award for Best Country Song has been awarded since 1965.\n- In 1968, O. C. Smith's recording of \"Little Green Apples\" reached No. 2 on the Billboard Hot 100 and sold over one million records.\n- Roger Miller's version of \"Little Green Apples\" became a Top 40 hit on the Billboard Hot 100 and on the UK Singles Chart.\n- Patti Page's version of \"Little Green Apples\" became her last entry on the Billboard Hot 100.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "20cbd4e3-0231-5c84-9877-f6007c5b8590",
        "text": "Page: Little Green Apples. Sentence: Miller's version became a Top 40 hit on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 chart and on the UK Singles Chart, while Page's version became her last Hot 100 entry and Smith's version became a No. 2 hit on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 chart.\nPage: Grammy Award for Best Country Song. Sentence: The Grammy Award for Best Country Song (sometimes known as the Country Songwriter's Award) has been awarded since 1965.\nPage: O. C. Smith. Sentence: His recording of \"Little Green Apples\" went to number 2 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 in 1968 and sold over one million records.",
